Imagine opening your design tool from ChatGPT's sidebar. Your projects are there. You select a design, ask the agent to change it, and keep working in the same canvas. The interface stays open as the conversation continues.


At OpenAI Dev Day, we spent time with the team behind **MCP Extensions** , the SDKs and specification that give plugins access to more of ChatGPT's interface. Users can launch an app directly or open a supported file in its editor. The app can also share the user's selection with the agent.


For software companies, this changes what an MCP integration can offer. A useful tool call might answer one question. A persistent workspace can support a whole editing session, with direct interaction when the user wants control and conversation when they want help.


We described this after Dev Day as ChatGPT becoming more like an operating system. Sidebar launchers and file handlers are familiar ways to reach software. The practical question for developers is which part of their product belongs in that environment.


This demo shows what Manufact looks like as an MCP plugin extension. We render the same page we host in[Manufact Analytics](https://manufact.com/platform/analytics) , so you can explore your MCP server's usage alongside the conversation.


[Watch the demo on YouTube](https://youtu.be/ahQLX0CNkR0)


## What MCP Extensions adds


[MCP Apps](https://manufact.com/blog/what-is-an-mcp-app) already provides the foundation for interactive UI: a tool points to an HTML resource, and the host renders it in a sandbox.[OpenAI MCP Extensions](https://github.com/openai/mcp-extensions) adds integration points specific to ChatGPT. It is a toolkit for building plugins, rather than a plugin your users install by itself.


The[mcp-use framework](https://manufact.com/blog/mcp-app-with-mcp-use) has first-class support for MCP Apps. You can test your MCP Apps with the[mcp-use Inspector](https://manufact.com/inspector) , previewing widgets and inspecting the tool calls that supply their data.


OpenAI's overview of the places a plugin can appear inside ChatGPT.


The main entry points answer different product needs:


Entry point How the user opens it A useful starting view


` global


`


Click your app in the sidebar A project library or dashboard


` thread


`


Open an app tab within a conversation The document or visualization being discussed


` file


`


Open a file with an extension your app handles A viewer or editor for that file


OpenAI's[Bits & Bolts example](https://github.com/openai/mcp-extensions/tree/main/plugins/bits-and-bolts) demonstrates a parts library and a CAD file viewer. Its source is a useful reference for how the UI connects to the server.


Extensions also cover searchable composer mentions and setup flows. OpenAI highlights Canva's sidebar experience, Figma's file mentions, and Adobe's file handlers in its[extension guide](https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions) .


These capabilities are host-specific. At launch, the[support matrix](https://github.com/openai/mcp-extensions/blob/main/docs/spec.md#platform-support) lists file entry points and composer mentions as desktop-only. Keep your underlying tools usable in other MCP clients and check capabilities before calling an optional frontend API.


